# Shared .dockerignore for the cowork repo. Build context is the cowork repo
# root, so both images (Dockerfile = all-in-one SPA+server; Dockerfile.frontend
# = static SPA on nginx) use this single file. **/ globs also cover nested
# subdirectories.

# Build artifacts: produced inside the image.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/out/
**/release/
**/build/

# Editor / OS / agent junk.
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/.cursor/
**/.claude/
**/*.swp

# Source-control internals: not needed for builds, and shipping .git leaks
# commit history.
**/.git/
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.github/

# Environment / secrets: never bake into images. The negation keeps the
# .env.example template available for docs/setup scripts.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# Python caches and local virtualenvs (relevant to the all-in-one build).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest-workspace/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/scratchpad-venvs/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*

# Runtime state directories: host data that must not be baked in.
**/.anton/
**/.cowork/

# Logs.
**/*.log
**/logs/

# Documentation drafts and the throwaway port-audit.
**/docs/web-port-audit.md
